// Security findings registry — one JSON object per line.
//
// This file is a whitelist of FACTS, in the same spirit as the protocol
// whitelist in src/protocols.py: an entry exists because a person put it here on
// purpose, with a source anyone can go and check.
//
// It is intentionally empty. An entry labelled CONFIRMED_INCIDENT is trusted by
// everything downstream — it can support a claim, raise a confidence score, and
// appear in a report as an established fact about a named protocol. Filling this
// in from memory or from an unverified summary would put defamatory content
// behind that label. Every entry needs a citation an operator has read.
//
// Adding one:
//
//   {"id": "unique-slug",
//    "protocol": "ethena",                    // must be in the whitelist
//    "classification": "confirmed_incident",  // confirmed_incident
//                                             // | known_vulnerability
//                                             // | suspicious_signal
//                                             // | unverified_claim
//    "title": "Short description",
//    "summary": "What happened, in a sentence or two.",
//    "source_uri": "https://...",             // where this is documented
//    "source_tier": "official",               // primary | official | community | unverified
//    "status": "mitigated",                   // active | mitigated | resolved | unknown
//    "occurred_at": "2026-01-15T00:00:00Z",   // optional
//    "disclosed_at": "2026-01-17T00:00:00Z",  // optional
//    "references": ["https://..."]}           // optional
//
// Classification and source_tier are INDEPENDENT. A confirmed incident reported
// by a community researcher is confirmed AND community-tier. Do not raise the
// tier to reflect how certain the finding is, or the classification to reflect
// how reputable the source is.
//
// Only confirmed_incident and known_vulnerability may support a finding.
// suspicious_signal and unverified_claim attach as neutral context: they will
// appear in the report and will never raise a confidence score.
